[01:09.67] Procession moves on, the shouting is over
[01:16.65] Praise to the glory of loved ones now gone
[01:24.66] Talking aloud as they sit round their tables
[01:31.81] 
[01:34.00] Scattering flowers washed down by the rain
[01:41.22] 
[01:44.37] Stood by the gate at the foot of the garden
[01:51.93] Watching them pass like clouds in the sky
[01:59.03] 
[02:01.60] Try to cry out in the heat of the moment
[02:08.60] 
[02:10.67] Possessed by a fury that burns from inside
[02:18.13] 
[03:29.65] Cry like a child, though these years make me older
[03:36.62] With children my time is so wastefully spent
[03:43.99] 
[03:46.00] A burden to keep, though their inner communion
[03:54.85] Accept like a curse an unlucky deal
[04:01.99] 
[04:04.01] Played by the gate at the foot of the garden
[04:12.67] My view stretches out from the fence to the wall
[04:21.11] No words could explain, no actions determine
[04:29.46] Just watching the trees and the leaves as they fall
[04:35.31] 